REFERENCE DATA
--------------

Shoalcheck carries tables of public upstream facts. They are facts, not authorship,
and each names its own source and the date it was generated:

  - cloud instance, storage and network prices (internal/pricing,
    internal/refdata) — from the providers' own public price lists
  - the Kubernetes API removal schedule (internal/apiremoval) — from the
    upstream deprecation policy and release notes
  - the per-provider Kubernetes support calendar (internal/kubeversions) —
    from each provider's published release and end-of-support dates

A rendered reading states which table it used and when that table was
generated, so a figure can be checked against its source rather than trusted.


THIRD-PARTY DEPENDENCIES
------------------------

Go module dependencies and their licences are declared in go.mod and go.sum.
`make depcheck` enforces the direction of the dependency graph; it does not
audit licences. The completion register's "Dependency licences — swept" row
records that sweep and its date.
